WEBVTT

NOTE Curiosity: Landing on Mars (NASA/JPL-Caltech, 2011), public domain. Captions describing what is on screen, written for the review home (the animation has no narration).

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.000
Earth from orbit, the Sun behind it.

2
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:23.000
The rocket's upper stage carries the spacecraft away from Earth.

3
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:35.000
The spacecraft separates from the upper stage.

4
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:47.000
The cruise stage's solar panels catch the sunlight.

5
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:59.000
Months of cruise through space toward Mars.

6
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:11.000
The capsule nears the red planet.

7
00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:23.000
Mars fills the view ahead.

8
00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:35.000
The capsule meets the thin Martian air.

9
00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:47.000
The heat shield glows as the capsule slows.

10
00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:59.000
The parachute opens high above the ground.

11
00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:11.000
The heat shield falls away toward the surface.

12
00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:23.000
The descent stage fires its rockets.

13
00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:35.000
The rover is carried down beneath the descent stage.

14
00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:47.000
The rover's wheels unfold.

15
00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:59.000
The sky crane lowers the rover on its cables.

16
00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:11.000
The rover hangs just above the ground.

17
00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:23.000
Touchdown. The descent stage flies off.

18
00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:35.000
Curiosity sits in Gale Crater, Mount Sharp behind it.

19
00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:47.000
The Sun rises over the crater's rim.

20
00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:59.000
A close look at the rover's deck.

21
00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:11.000
Dusk on Mars, the rover in the low light.

22
00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:23.000
The mast camera looks around for the first time.

23
00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:35.000
A wide, empty plain stretches to the hills.

24
00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:47.000
The mast's cameras and laser turn toward the view.

25
00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:59.000
The hills of the crater, seen from the rover.

26
00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:11.000
An orbiter passes overhead to relay the rover's data.

27
00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:23.000
Curiosity faces the camera.

28
00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:35.000
The six wheels roll over the rocks.

29
00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:47.000
Layered hills rise from the crater floor.

30
00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:59.000
The rover stops at the foot of the hills.

31
00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:11.000
The mast rises over the rover's body.

32
00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:23.000
Far off, the rover crosses the dunes.

33
00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:35.000
The rover drives across a slope.

34
00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:47.000
The mast looks back along the rover.

35
00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:59.000
The rover, close up, among the rocks.

36
00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:11.000
Its wheel tracks run back across the plain.

37
00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:23.000
A field of dunes, and the mountain beyond.

38
00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:35.000
The mast camera studies the ground ahead.

39
00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:47.000
The rover pauses on the slope.

40
00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:59.000
It climbs toward the layers of the mountain.

41
00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:11.000
The mast against the hills.

42
00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:23.000
The robotic arm reaches out.

43
00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:35.000
The arm's tools turn over a rock.

44
00:08:36.000 --> 00:08:47.000
The arm presses against the rock face.

45
00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:59.000
The drill bites into the rock.

46
00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:11.000
The rover holds its arm out over the ground.

47
00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:23.000
The arm brings the sample to the rover's deck.

48
00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:35.000
The deck opens to take the sample in.

49
00:09:36.000 --> 00:09:47.000
Inside, the sample drops into an instrument.

50
00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:59.000
A beam of light inside the laboratory.

51
00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:11.000
The laser strikes a rock to read what it is made of.

52
00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:23.000
A look inside the rover's instruments.

53
00:10:24.000 --> 00:10:35.000
The mast and the deck, work done.

54
00:10:36.000 --> 00:10:47.000
The rover drives on.

55
00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:59.000
Curiosity heads toward the camera.

56
00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:11.000
The dunes and the mountain ahead of it.
